1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,470
Welcome to Manham Port, where a thousand years of history are brought to life.

2
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:08,514
All the family can enjoy a day out at Manham:

3
00:00:08,514 --> 00:00:14,282
visit our copper mine, see models of the machinery it used, have your photo

4
00:00:14,282 --> 00:00:21,232
taken in nineteenth-century costume, experience at first hand how people lived at different stages

5
00:00:21,232 --> 00:00:22,153
throughout history,

6
00:00:22,153 --> 00:00:27,340
and especially how children studied, worked and played.

7
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:33,928
The port of Manham is located in beautiful and peaceful countryside, on a bend

8
00:00:33,928 --> 00:00:35,310
in the great River Avon,

9
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:40,577
and developed here because it's the highest navigable point of the Avon - boats

10
00:00:40,577 --> 00:00:44,922
can go no higher up this river - and proved a handy place to load

11
00:00:44,922 --> 00:00:47,726
and unload cargo to and from the sea,

12
00:00:47,726 --> 00:00:50,890
which is over 23 miles away.

13
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:57,604
A small port was already established here when, about 900 years ago, tin was

14
00:00:57,604 --> 00:01:01,592
discovered nearby, though it wasn't until the Industrial Revolution,

15
00:01:01,592 --> 00:01:05,320
when a tremendous need for metals of all kinds developed,

16
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:09,990
that Manham expanded to become one of the busiest ports in the country.

17
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:15,184
And because it was already so busy, prospectors began to look for other minerals,

18
00:01:15,184 --> 00:01:20,038
and by the end of the nineteenth century, lead, copper, manganese

19
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:24,490
and arsenic were added to the cargos leaving Manham.

20
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:27,906
In the early days, the ores had been smelted -

21
00:01:27,906 --> 00:01:31,080
or processed - in the same area they were mined.

22
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:36,931
But, as demand grew, the smelting process required huge factory furnaces

23
00:01:36,931 --> 00:01:41,419
or fires to melt the metal from the rock and there was not enough

24
00:01:41,419 --> 00:01:42,902
coal in the local area,

25
00:01:42,902 --> 00:01:47,130
so the rocks containing minerals had to be shipped Iong distances.

26
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:52,933
Sadly, in the twentieth century, the great port of Manham declined,

27
00:01:52,933 --> 00:01:57,410
and thousands of workers were forced to emigrate out of the area.

28
00:01:57,410 --> 00:01:59,844
The building at the port fell into disrepair,

29
00:01:59,844 --> 00:02:02,800
and the place became almost forgotten.

30
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:07,968
But then, the Manham Trust was formed to conserve the historical resources of the

31
00:02:07,968 --> 00:02:08,390
area.

32
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:15,381
It organised scores of local volunteers to remove undergrowth to find the original outlines

33
00:02:15,381 --> 00:02:17,410
of the installations.

34
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:24,118
It then brought in paid professionals to match installations with maps of the original port complex

35
00:02:24,118 --> 00:02:26,890
and to set about reconstructing it.

36
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:32,720
Today you can see the results of this ambitious programme of restoration.

37
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:33,783
The intention,

38
00:02:33,783 --> 00:02:37,472
and we believe this will be realised before the end of the year, is

39
00:02:37,472 --> 00:02:42,165
to return Manham Port to the condition it reached at its peak as 'the

40
00:02:42,165 --> 00:02:44,270
greatest copper port in the country'.

41
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:49,170
But what can you do and see on your visit today?

42
00:02:49,170 --> 00:02:50,497
Here are just a few highlights.

43
00:02:50,497 --> 00:02:54,800
We suggest you start with the visit to the copper mine.

44
00:02:54,800 --> 00:03:00,867
Travel on converted mining trains and journey into the depths of the mountain along

45
00:03:00,867 --> 00:03:03,900
seams once worked by hundreds of miners.

46
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:09,180
Watch out especially for the great pumping machines which rid the mine of water.

47
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:14,689
But please be warned that, like all mines, ours is very dark and closed in

48
00:03:14,689 --> 00:03:19,831
and we do say that children under five and also dogs should NOT be

49
00:03:19,831 --> 00:03:21,300
taken into the mine.

50
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:26,140
The next recommended visit is to the village school.

51
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:30,237
While looking round the classrooms, take a special look at our display of games,

52
00:03:30,237 --> 00:03:32,870
which is one of the largest in the world.

53
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:38,260
And it's recommended that you time your visit to coincide with a guided tour.

54
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:41,980
This will give you the opportunity to ask lots of questions.

55
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:47,080
Near the school is the beautiful old sailing ketch called The George'.

56
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:51,110
You are welcome to board the boat and look round the cabins.

57
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:55,267
Look out for the ship's wheel which was missing until only five years ago

58
00:03:55,267 --> 00:03:58,830
when it was dredged out of the silt by a local fisherman.

59
00:03:58,830 --> 00:04:02,561
We have no idea how it got there but it's been polished

60
00:04:02,561 --> 00:04:05,670
and proudly restored to its original place on the boat.

61
00:04:05,670 --> 00:04:09,635
Please take care going down the ladders if you wish to visit the lower

62
00:04:09,635 --> 00:04:12,750
deck - we don't recommend you allow young children to use them.

63
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:16,334
So we hope you have a memorable visit to Manham Port

64
00:04:16,334 --> 00:04:18,940
and will tell your friends all about us.
